    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing our highest offensive floor; despite a left-on-left disadvantage against Rojas, his elite .425 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against a 5.83 xERA starter push him to a 75.61 score. Our pursuit of the scarcest category, stolen bases, remains centered on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.61) and **Colt Keith** (69.13). While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is buried in the 8-hole, his dynamic platoon advantage against Sproat makes him a high-efficiency play for speed, whereas **Colt Keith** benefits from a premium leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Cecconi. Conversely, **Trea Turner** (66.72) remains a mandatory start due to his leadoff role and consistent volume, even against a tough arm like Lodolo.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles, notably **Christian Yelich** (50.67), who struggles against the platoon profile of Imanaga, and **Dillon Dingler** (48.44), whose dynamic platoon penalty narrowly keeps him above our bench threshold. The most difficult decision rested with the utility slot; while **Casey Schmitt** (61.88) earned his place today thanks to a significant boost from his platoon matchup against Gallen, he narrowly edged out our depth options. We are monitoring the status of **Lars Nootbaar** and **Zac Veen**, both of whom remain unavailable due to IL and minor league assignments, respectively, limiting our flexibility. Given that **Kyle Schwarber** and **Caleb Durbin** are not in the official lineup, we are relying on our core to compensate for the lack of bench depth today. Risk mitigation is focused on the lower-order volatility of **Hyeseong Kim**, who faces a high-efficiency hold pitcher in King, putting his 47.68 score on the thin edge of our starting criteria.",
